A||||10||Brian87egotrip||Drove car over 200 miles no oil!||||1||
Z||000000||Brian87egotrip||12-09-2001||06:12 PM||||On the way home from A fiero get together a fellow club member noticed I was making his car oily.  We drove for a while and decided to check my oil.  On boy there was none.  Bone dry. Thank God for synthitec oil.  Put some oil in amde it home with out a problem. Yeah!!  Next week I'll tell ya about Driving my car with tire pressure 30psi below what it should be.  Have a great holiday season, and happy new years.<P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT<BR>http://floridafieros.org/daytona<BR>2002||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jake_Dragon||12-09-2001||06:20 PM||||There goes the ground water.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>I did the same thing about 2 months ago.<BR>Turned out when I changed the oil filter I didn't get to old gasket off. <BR>It spit all the oil out in less than a 1/4 mile.<BR>I dumped 4 quarts in and drove the 1/2 mile home.<BR>Took the filter off and removed the old gasket, put the filter back on I'm back on the road.||||reg||1
