Z||000005||Butter||12-10-2001||03:50 PM||||Must have had some oil in it cause the fuel pump is hooked up to the oil pressure sending unit and if the oil pressure drops out the fuel pump shuts down.<P>Have you disable this circuit?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/buttersig_1.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000006||Brian87egotrip||12-10-2001||04:47 PM||||Butter, I don't think it is disabled.  All I know is that when we checked the oil 4 times the dipstick came out dry. We let the car set for a bit before we checked it. OIl guage doesn't work right i believe.  It was bouncing all over the place.  <P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT<BR>http://floridafieros.org/daytona<BR>2002||||reg||1
Z||000007||Rodrv6||12-10-2001||09:00 PM||||Butter--it's a common misconception that low oil pressure will turn off the fuel pump.  As long as the fuel pump relay is working correctly the engine will continue to run without oil pressure until it melts down.  The switch in the oil pressure switch is there to operate the fuel pump if the relay goes bad.  You can unplug the oil pressure switch on any year and engine on the Fiero and start and run the engine--If the relay is good.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000008||BlackStang95||12-11-2001||03:29 AM||||Even though the dipstick was dry you might have had some oil (quart or two) in there.  Still very lucky to have no immediate damage, synthentic oil is good. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||ITB 2M4||12-11-2001||02:25 PM||||If you unhook the oil pressure sending unit in my '84, the motor shuts off right away.<P>And, in a similar story, I once drove my '81 X-11 from Corpus Christi, Tx., to Tampa, Fl. with no tranny fluid! I was 19 at the time, and just had the CV joints replaced, and never thought about checking to see if the work was done right.  The last 100 miles into Tampa, it would only stay in fourth gear (4-spd.), without having to hold it in gear, and howled pretty good in the other three.  Used up all $680 I had in savings to get it fixed!  But what a great testament to GM transmissions.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4<BR>AOL IM- DGPFiero||||reg||4
